 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the local finance law, in relation to the issuance of bonds to finance airport improvements at the East Hampton Airport",
    "basePrintNo": "S3690",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3690-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11.00, Loc Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Local Finance Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3690\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the local finance law, in relation to\nthe issuance of bonds to finance airport improvements at the East\nHampton Airport\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation authorizes the issuance of bonds by the Town of East\nHampton to finance airport improvements at the East Hampton Airport\nfor a period not to exceed 30 years.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nParagraph a of Section 11.00 of the Local Finance Law is amended by\nadding a new subdivision 14-a relating to the issuance of bonds by the\nTown of East Hampton to finance airport improvements at the East\nHampton Airport for a period not to exceed 30 years.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of East Hampton owns and operates the East Hampton Airport,\nlocated in the Town of East Hampton, hamlet of Wainscott. The Town's\ngrant assurances from the Federal Aviation Administration expired on\nDecember 31, 2014, and as such, the Town no longer. obtains FAA\nfunding for the operation and maintenance of the airport. The Town\nwill now assume all responsibility to finance airport capital\nprojects.\n\nCurrent local finance law defines the maximum amortization period for\nairport projects as 10 years. This legislation is necessary to allow\nthe Town to bond out improvements over a longer period of time.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2015: New Legislation\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
